+---
+id: dl-004-bulk-import-is-line-based-tolerant-of-omitted-fields-and-keeps-going-after-a-bad-line
+type: decision-log
+title: "Bulk import is line-based, tolerant of omitted fields, and keeps going after a bad line"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Context
+Teams move from spreadsheets to Tidy Tasks and need a bulk import with a per-line report.
+
+## Decision
+One task per line, `title;priority;tags`; lines split on `\n` or `\r\n`. Priority and tags may be
+omitted (a line with only a title, or title and priority, is valid); an empty priority is `normal`;
+tags are split on whitespace. More than three fields is rejected, since a `;` in a title would silently
+shift fields. Priority is trimmed but otherwise strict (`High` is rejected). A line failing validation
+or duplicating a title is rejected with the domain's message, and the import goes on. Blank lines are
+skipped but counted in line numbers, so they match the spreadsheet rows. Parsing is in the domain and
+never throws (r4); the import is not atomic.
+
+## Consequences
+A partly bad file imports its good lines; callers show `rejected` to the user. Titles cannot contain `;`.
